      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "There are few data about lipid profiles in unselected patients with angiographically confirmed coronary artery disease (CAD)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "HYPOTHESIS",
          "content": "The study was undertaken to investigate the demographics, clinical characteristics, angiographic findings, and baseline lipid status of 1,000 consecutive unselected patients with angiographically confirmed CAD."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "Between April 2001 and July 2002, we obtained informed consent and prospectively collected clinical characteristics, fasting lipid profiles, and angiographic results from 1,000 sequential patients with CAD confirmed by angiography."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "In these patients with confirmed CAD, 78% had history of hyperlipidemia. Although 62% were receiving lipid-lowering therapy, only 46% had a low-density lipoprotein target of < 100 mg/dl, and only 20% had achieved all four National Cholesterol Education Program-recommended lipid targets."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "Better strategies to ensure optimal lipid levels are required. One such method using computerized workflow is being evaluated in this population."
        }
      ]},
